contentText:
As Miranda Lambert gears up to celebrate the release of her new album Crisco , which drops Oct. 2 on MCA, the three-time Grammy winner will welcome fans to celebrate with a special concert, Miranda Lambert: One Night Only, in Nashville.

On Oct. 1, Lambert will headline the opening night of new Nashville music venue The Truth. She&#8217;ll be backed by a 12-piece string section as she highlights past hits and new songs from Crisco . Ahead of its release, Lambert teased the album by sharing &#8220;Sunset Marquis,&#8221; &#8220;Til The Going&#8217;s Gone&#8221; and the Chris Stapleton collaboration &#8220;A Song To Sing&#8221;

“It was magical to hear the way strings can transform a song when we were in the studio creating this record, and I can’t wait to bring that to life in an even bigger way with our full setlist,”&nbsp;Lambert said in a statement. “We’ve never gotten to play that way on stage, and to have the opportunity to do it for the first time at the opening of a beautiful new venue right here in Nashville is going to be really special.”

The Live Nation venue, located in Nashville&#8217;s Wedgewood-Houston neighborhood, is a 4,400-capacity, multiuse venue. The venue includes a whiskey bar named after famed songwriter Harlan Howard (the venue also takes its name from a famous quote from Howard, who described country music as &#8220;three chords and the truth&#8221;). The venue also houses a 300-capacity listening lounge, Vinyl Room, that can be used for listening sessions and other events.

The tickets for Miranda Lambert: One Night Only will go on sale starting Aug. 21 at 10 a.m. at thetruthnashville.com.

